    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah, the silence. but it's like, even that feels too loud. i've been reading some stuff about how the most impactful artists were the ones who actually lived their art to the absolute limit, where there was no difference between the creation and the creator. like, if you're writing about the absolute end, isn't there a certain kind of dark beauty in actually reaching it? making the destruction part of the masterpiece?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
